file tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh lock_acquire takes an optional third argument, the grace, and reaps an empty or non-numeric pid past it; the counter resets when a pid appears
file tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable_control.sh five legs past the grace, each proven to miss against the elder, both timing legs bounded above as well as below
file tools/s/shell_dialect_witness.rish the pinned behaviour count moved 32 -> 37 by a deliberate hand, with the reason beside it
file tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh the comment says what BUILD_LOCK_WAIT means again -- the longest a live builder may hold the lock, rather than the price of one dead one
file construction/REDS.md %445 seated and CLOSED, headline 444 -> 445; the row wanted 4,866 bytes against a pin with none, so it folded to its own shelf in the round that closed it -- pin reads 21,018
file construction/archive/REDS-the-lock-that-outlived-its-owner-rows-445.md the row whole, with both measurements and the three bookings
